+
+## Rate limiting
+
+Every request except `GET /health` is limited per `x-api-key` header value. Requests without the header share the key `anonymous`.
+
+The limiter runs before routing and authentication, so requests that end in 401, 403 or 404 also count.
+
+Configure it with `createServer({ rateLimit: { limit, windowMs } })`. The default is `{ limit: 60, windowMs: 60000 }`. Partial objects merge with the defaults. Timing uses the server's `now` option.
+
+Windows are fixed: a key's window starts at its first request and lasts `windowMs`. The first `limit` requests in it are allowed. The first request at or after `windowStart + windowMs` starts a new window.
+
+Every limited response has:
+
+- `X-RateLimit-Limit`: the limit.
+- `X-RateLimit-Remaining`: requests left in the current window after this one, never below 0.
+
+Rejected requests get `429`, a `Retry-After` header (whole seconds until the window ends, rounded up, at least 1) and the body `{"error":"rate_limited","retryAfter":<seconds>}`.
+
+`GET /health` is exempt: it is never rejected, never counted and has no rate-limit headers.
